Different IT fields must work together to make a secure national login service work. Software enables the user to log in to government websites and applications. Artificial intelligence can identify anything that seems unusual in your logins, but it can still be flawed, so it's important to review the results. Android permissions are a way to regulate access to various information that a mobile app can access. Networking makes it possible for devices to link to online services. While DNS over HTTPS (DoH) is a beneficial measure to prevent DNS queries from being easily monitored during their journey over the network, it is not a means of hiding all user activity. Cybersecurity measures are put in place to safeguard accounts from attackers, and data protection measures are implemented to keep citizens' data safe. Combined, these six areas can improve the safety and reliability of the service. Being part of the networking design, it is crucial to grasp both advantages and limitations of DoH.
